          "id": "chem-cu-q3",
          "number": "3",
          "question": "Write down the chemistry of blue vitriol.",
          "answer": "Blue vitriol is **hydrated copper (II) sulphate, $\\text{CuSO}_4\\cdot 5\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$**.\n- **Structure:** Four water molecules are coordinated to the central $\\text{Cu}^{2+}$ ion in a square planar geometry, while the fifth water molecule is hydrogen-bonded between coordinated water and sulphate ions: $[\\text{Cu}(\\text{H}_2\\text{O})_4]\\text{SO}_4\\cdot \\text{H}_2\\text{O}$.\n- **Action of Heat:**\n$$\\text{CuSO}_4\\cdot 5\\text{H}_2\\text{O} \\xrightarrow{100^\\circ\\text{C}} \\text{CuSO}_4\\cdot \\text{H}_2\\text{O} \\xrightarrow{230^\\circ\\text{C}} \\text{CuSO}_4 \\text{ (white anhydrous)} \\xrightarrow{750^\\circ\\text{C}} \\text{CuO} + \\text{SO}_2 + \\frac{1}{2}\\text{O}_2$$"
